WEBVTT

00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:02.030
You're good at the work.

00:00:02.146 --> 00:00:03.295
That was never the problem.

00:00:03.748 --> 00:00:05.420
You finish at six, and somebody still

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:07.208
has to answer the comment, ring back

00:00:07.254 --> 00:00:09.541
whoever asked about pricing, and fill next

00:00:09.576 --> 00:00:10.459
week's diary.

00:00:10.853 --> 00:00:12.235
So it doesn't get done.

00:00:12.455 --> 00:00:13.616
Not because you're lazy.

00:00:13.837 --> 00:00:15.857
Because you already have a job.

00:00:16.557 --> 00:00:17.985
So we build the whole thing.

00:00:18.206 --> 00:00:20.504
We rebuilt BrightCover's website from scratch.

00:00:20.655 --> 00:00:22.861
Fast, works on a phone, every button

00:00:22.977 --> 00:00:25.067
doing one thing: book you in, or

00:00:25.137 --> 00:00:25.810
send the guide.

00:00:25.984 --> 00:00:27.331
They book, and it lands in one

00:00:27.366 --> 00:00:28.980
place, with their name and where they've

00:00:29.014 --> 00:00:29.583
got to.

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:32.347
One screen, everybody who ever asked.

00:00:33.047 --> 00:00:34.336
Then the part that gives you your

00:00:34.405 --> 00:00:35.183
evenings back.

00:00:35.404 --> 00:00:38.144
Someone comments, messages, texts, or opens the

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:39.200
chat on your site.

00:00:39.595 --> 00:00:41.162
They get an answer in seconds.

00:00:41.337 --> 00:00:44.611
Facebook, Instagram, WhatsApp, text, the website.

00:00:44.947 --> 00:00:46.178
It offers them a time.

00:00:46.515 --> 00:00:48.129
And when someone asks a price, or

00:00:48.198 --> 00:00:50.555
anything regulated, it stops and passes it

00:00:50.602 --> 00:00:50.985
to you.

00:00:51.438 --> 00:00:53.435
That's the part most people skip.

00:00:54.135 --> 00:00:55.853
Being good is no use if nobody

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:56.608
can find you.

00:00:57.061 --> 00:00:58.558
Three ways people look now.

00:00:58.733 --> 00:00:59.534
They search.

00:00:59.824 --> 00:01:01.159
They read the answer at the top.

00:01:01.275 --> 00:01:02.622
Or they ask their phone and take

00:01:02.645 --> 00:01:03.388
what it says.

00:01:03.725 --> 00:01:05.246
So we put her where those answers

00:01:05.304 --> 00:01:08.253
come from: Google across fifteen cities, Yelp,

00:01:08.276 --> 00:01:08.845
and Bing.

00:01:09.298 --> 00:01:11.132
Bing is what those assistants read.

00:01:11.832 --> 00:01:13.283
Then you need something to say.

00:01:13.457 --> 00:01:14.073
Every day.

00:01:14.467 --> 00:01:15.245
Forever.

00:01:15.768 --> 00:01:17.463
That's where most of this falls over.

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:19.030
So we built that.

00:01:19.367 --> 00:01:20.470
She has never stood in front of

00:01:20.505 --> 00:01:21.085
a camera.

00:01:21.306 --> 00:01:23.303
Fourteen films in two weeks.

00:01:23.639 --> 00:01:25.462
Her face, her voice, a different room

00:01:25.555 --> 00:01:26.286
every time.

00:01:26.623 --> 00:01:29.351
Posting six times a day since, untouched.

00:01:29.804 --> 00:01:32.080
Twenty times that without you hiring anyone.

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:34.603
Same machine, your words.

00:01:34.998 --> 00:01:37.354
A medspa fills next week's empty chairs.

00:01:37.575 --> 00:01:39.537
A salon rebooks before they leave.

00:01:39.874 --> 00:01:42.138
An accountant books January in November.

00:01:42.532 --> 00:01:44.448
A group home answers the nine o'clock

00:01:44.506 --> 00:01:44.924
call.

00:01:45.261 --> 00:01:47.432
A realtor, a caterer, a cleaner, a

00:01:47.548 --> 00:01:48.233
food truck.

00:01:48.407 --> 00:01:49.475
Give us twenty minutes.

00:01:49.649 --> 00:01:51.124
Let's give you your time back, while

00:01:51.147 --> 00:01:52.285
we grow your business.
